[{:db/id "q-161314/selection/ba447814f6c9c26bad0985dfb9b1cfe7471db81e108ffc582c1a3edb06c8cbbd" :answer/id #uuid "d38174c0-8e72-51c0-8e3f-b2f2817cb331" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}(-{x}^{2}y-{x}^{2}y)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161314/selection/e4d92fba2aafdfc3c9e82272c51df51a3d450409dcde87e81478769a4d0b583f" :answer/id #uuid "5c17e748-6eb7-56df-83d3-1283719b064b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3x}({x}^{3}y+{x}^{2}{y}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161314/selection/c734ed1bda080369697543ca9102de2b0a109396523bb5452a74d3b7b476da69" :answer/id #uuid "dd2c9b30-b6a9-51e5-8ae1-0b6004bed209" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}(-{x}^{3}y+{x}^{2}{y}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161314/selection/55c53fa9fe45f9c62b77a29bb646d575ce5d97a8fd408f6553ca30869eee70aa" :answer/id #uuid "73727ed4-503d-5ff7-98f9-a00067c5f5f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}(-{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}{y}^{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161314/selection/731d81c50e6ff5c9701d3806fbe99a1a7bf91bea7df13eec818d5a6c93d770ad" :answer/id #uuid "b8fe9fe2-cf76-5882-b7d7-7b11eee05aae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3y}(-{x}^{2}y-{x}^{2}{y}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161314/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b9a22bb3-ef48-564c-8e4c-9289e971998a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161314/selection/c734ed1bda080369697543ca9102de2b0a109396523bb5452a74d3b7b476da69" :answer-field/choices ["q-161314/selection/ba447814f6c9c26bad0985dfb9b1cfe7471db81e108ffc582c1a3edb06c8cbbd" "q-161314/selection/e4d92fba2aafdfc3c9e82272c51df51a3d450409dcde87e81478769a4d0b583f" "q-161314/selection/c734ed1bda080369697543ca9102de2b0a109396523bb5452a74d3b7b476da69" "q-161314/selection/55c53fa9fe45f9c62b77a29bb646d575ce5d97a8fd408f6553ca30869eee70aa" "q-161314/selection/731d81c50e6ff5c9701d3806fbe99a1a7bf91bea7df13eec818d5a6c93d770ad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161314" :question/id #uuid "d8e5c369-0d01-5527-87a6-9d6d08f8cf0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-161314" :question/problem "Consider the surface integral of the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}yz,$ where the surface $S$ is defined by $z=-x+y$ for $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$\nThis surface integral can be written as a repeated integral, as shown below. \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=g(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFor the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-x+y)=-1,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-x+y)=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(-1)}^{2}+{(1)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,{x}^{2}y(-x+y)\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\sqrt{3}(-{x}^{3}y+{x}^{2}{y}^{2})\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161314/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8885504f-07fb-5308-a982-608d7baa262b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161314"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161321/selection/be42141f30f2baacd7cbc60c8b14a4e7006b67bec451c2bba00116ef53226221" :answer/id #uuid "9c1f3deb-ab05-5305-a5c8-cdf55cc61c9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}+x{y}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161321/selection/eedc70c3f84e0b0adec05caa84c9db44b80a3d103629a1870e7d87e3b3c69658" :answer/id #uuid "33556c58-5986-5fdc-854f-f02535d36c3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{5}({x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161321/selection/9ed9d586a90e9c8d518a600da11b1c33c3c585f927a16687c36f41a9b4ac6fdc" :answer/id #uuid "f77db71b-52e1-578b-9270-b94ffb549cca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}({x}^{2}y+{x}^{2}{y}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161321/selection/5ede1f0e0889bb43b4647c5146088eb49fec89f470211825db85d63cc955e12c" :answer/id #uuid "4cc36e3b-226b-56be-b092-5c93631e88bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5x}(2{x}^{2}-x{y}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161321/selection/41277e34272ec89667b73bc95bf7421185bb023e2d0b449386cb571b800ad53a" :answer/id #uuid "7d72d6e2-1967-5bb8-9d8d-9b16cc1fd732" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{2}({x}^{2}y-x{y}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161321/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c9da3ad5-2372-5bf4-ab41-2c9090987fe5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161321/selection/eedc70c3f84e0b0adec05caa84c9db44b80a3d103629a1870e7d87e3b3c69658" :answer-field/choices ["q-161321/selection/be42141f30f2baacd7cbc60c8b14a4e7006b67bec451c2bba00116ef53226221" "q-161321/selection/eedc70c3f84e0b0adec05caa84c9db44b80a3d103629a1870e7d87e3b3c69658" "q-161321/selection/9ed9d586a90e9c8d518a600da11b1c33c3c585f927a16687c36f41a9b4ac6fdc" "q-161321/selection/5ede1f0e0889bb43b4647c5146088eb49fec89f470211825db85d63cc955e12c" "q-161321/selection/41277e34272ec89667b73bc95bf7421185bb023e2d0b449386cb571b800ad53a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161321" :question/id #uuid "9c54ec01-82a8-5a6f-92e4-d3028c762159" :question/math-academy-id "q-161321" :question/problem "Consider the surface integral of the function $f(x,y,z)=\\sqrt{2}xyz,$ where the surface $S$ is defined by $z=-\\sqrt{2}x-\\sqrt{2}y$ for $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$\nThis surface integral can be written as a repeated integral, as shown below. \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=g(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFor the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-\\sqrt{2}x-\\sqrt{2}y)=-\\sqrt{2},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-\\sqrt{2}x-\\sqrt{2}y)=-\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(-\\sqrt{2})}^{2}+{(-\\sqrt{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\sqrt{2}xy(-\\sqrt{2}x-\\sqrt{2}y)\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(-2{x}^{2}y-2x{y}^{2})\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,-2\\sqrt{5}({x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2})\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161321/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8885504f-07fb-5308-a982-608d7baa262b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161321"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161320/selection/de70e9586d24f4531de7aead9eca871c1661378aaf558c80bde4b8a3ba0e97f0" :answer/id #uuid "30426714-531a-557b-bd72-0179ad23e2b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({y}^{2}-{x}^{2}{y}^{4})\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161320/selection/0